+# Member chat fixture
+
+This fixture compiles the actual members page, ChatTab, TabBar, AppBar, member state,
+and existing sibling panels. The page receives synthetic `$app/stores` data and a
+deterministic gateway adapter. The page's real initialization and panel mounting
+run; no authentication, gateway session, provider call, or backend is involved.
+The adapter records UI activation and simulates pending sends. It does not qualify
+the production service's request admission, session fencing, or delivery.
+
+Use the installed native Vite/Svelte/Tailwind toolchain. The builder loads no app
+environment or Vite configuration, denies native network calls, uses private
+caches, and requires a fresh output below the candidate's sibling `chat-output`.
+Run one compiler with an external 120-second deadline and a 2-GiB Node heap. The
+artifact is limited to 550 files and 50 MiB, includes the real locally referenced
+fonts, and records hashes for actual source modules and every static member.
+
+The browser spec selects only that built manifest on a literal-loopback server.
+It denies other origins, uses one browser worker, and records actual browser,
+viewport, theme, native error, and request observations per case. A private
+Playwright config must select Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit explicitly; individual
+project runs are diagnostics, not a complete matrix. Browser-cache and optional
+WebKit executable settings come from the root's qualified private runtime receipt.
+
+The input cases dispatch synthetic composition KeyboardEvents to exercise the
+component's browser event boundary. They are not evidence of a real operating
+system IME session. Native keyboard navigation, focus, dimensions, scrolling, and
+CSS rendering are observed directly. Mobile viewport emulation does not qualify
+physical-device virtual keyboards or safe-area behavior.
+
+Final geometry requires all seven installed Barlow family/weight faces to load;
+the artifact carries their exact combined license notice. The earlier explicitly
+selected fallback-font baseline is diagnostic evidence only. Spanish cases use
+the actual Paraglide runtime and generated messages; they do not qualify localized
+URL routing, server hooks, or authenticated sessions.
+
+The normal matrix has twelve cases per engine: eight viewport/theme combinations,
+composition/newline handling, manual tab activation, live viewport resizing, and
+Spanish streaming/reduced-motion behavior. `MEMBER_CHAT_BASELINE=1` adds four
+diagnostic cases for the original components; these are not final acceptance.
+Every case attaches its actual browser, fonts, request observations and screenshot.
+Baseline and final command receipts stay outside the application tree; the root
+records independent acceptance.
+
+TabBar uses native buttons because the installed `@minion-stack/ui` 0.1.0 Button
+overwrites forwarded `role` and `tabindex` with link-specific defaults. Ordinary
+chat send continues to use that shared Button. This fixture does not substitute a
+different package or claim that the underlying primitive was repaired.
